# 🔍 Code Quality & SOLID Principles Audit
## Event Management Backend — PERN Stack

**Auditor:** Senior Code Reviewer (15+ years Node.js/Express/PostgreSQL)  
**Scope:** ~15,000+ lines across 25+ backend files  
**Date:** February 2026

---

## 📋 Executive Summary

| Metric | Score | Grade |
|--------|-------|-------|
| **Overall Code Quality** | **72/100** | **B−** |
| Error Handling | 82/100 | B+ |
| Naming & Readability | 70/100 | B− |
| Security | 78/100 | B |
| Performance | 75/100 | B |
| Testing Readiness | 40/100 | D |
| Documentation | 68/100 | C+ |
| SOLID Compliance | 58/100 | C |
| DRY / KISS | 55/100 | C− |

**Verdict:** This is a **functional, working production codebase** with competent architecture for its scale. It has clear separation of concerns (controllers → services → helpers), good error hierarchy, and smart performance optimizations (raw SQL, caching, `Promise.all`). However, it suffers from **massive file sizes, heavy code duplication, poor testability, and several SOLID violations** that will compound technical debt as features grow. The code is better than most university/startup backends — but it's **not yet production-grade for a system serving 25k users**.

---

## ⚖️ SOLID Principles Evaluation

### S — Single Responsibility Principle: **5/10** ⚠️

| File | Lines | Responsibilities | Violation? |
|------|-------|------------------|------------|
| [event.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/event.service.js) | 1279 | Event CRUD, listing, registration, statistics, volunteer re-exports, cache invalidation, visibility filtering, raw SQL | **Yes — God Service** |
| [team.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/team.service.js) | 1676 | Team CRUD, invitations, join requests, member removal, cancellation, lookingForTeammates, finalization | **Yes — too many concerns** |
| [stall.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/controllers/stall.controller.js) | 919 | Application CRUD, review, bulk updates, stall CRUD, toggle portal | **Borderline** |
| [event.controller.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/controllers/event.controller.js) | 869 | 15+ endpoints: list, get, update, publish, register, stats, QR scan, volunteers, registrations | **Yes** |
| [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js) | 857 | JWT auth, role gating, department perms, IPR perms, research perms, DSW perms, gate entry, event perms, ownership checks | **Yes — Swiss Army Knife** |
| [event.routes.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/routes/event.routes.js) | 624 | Every single route for events, teams, payments, stalls, settings, emails, coupons, prizes, custom fields — all in one file | **Yes** |

**Key Issue:** [event.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/event.service.js) at 1,279 lines is a **"God Service"** — it handles event creation, listing, registration, statistics, volunteer management, caching, and raw SQL queries. This makes it extremely hard to test, reason about, or modify safely.

**Recommendation:**
```
event.service.js (1279 lines) → Split into:
├── event-crud.service.js      (~200 lines)
├── event-listing.service.js   (~200 lines)
├── event-stats.service.js     (~150 lines)
├── event-registration.service.js (already partially done)
├── volunteer.service.js       (already exists)
└── cache.service.js           (~100 lines)
```

