### O — Open/Closed Principle: **6/10**

**What's good:**
- [asyncHandler](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/asyncHandler.js#1-17) is a clean higher-order function — open for extension
- [AppError](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/AppError.js#10-19) class hierarchy ([ValidationError](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/AppError.js#23-28), [ForbiddenError](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/AppError.js#41-46), [NotFoundError](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/AppError.js#50-55)) is well-designed and extensible
- [errorHandler.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/errorHandler.js) has a clean switch-like pattern for Prisma, Postgres, JWT errors — easy to add new handlers
- [checkPermission](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js#503-601) and [checkAnyPermission](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js#602-694) accept options objects — extensible without modifying internals

**What's problematic:**
- The [allowEventScan](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/routes/event.routes.js#65-109) middleware in [event.routes.js:68-108](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/routes/event.routes.js#L68-L108) is a **route-embedded authorization function** that queries the database. Adding new scan-permission sources requires modifying this function directly instead of registering new strategies.
- [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js) has **hardcoded permission lists** like `CHAIRPERSON_ALLOWED_PERMISSIONS` (lines 562-567). Adding new chairperson capabilities requires modifying the auth middleware source code.
- [formatEventResponse](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/utils/eventHelpers.js#369-481) in [eventHelpers.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/utils/eventHelpers.js) (lines 377-480) is a ~100-line function that manually maps every field. Adding a new event field requires finding this function and adding a line — no auto-mapping or schema-driven approach.

---

### L — Liskov Substitution Principle: **7/10** ✅

**Good:** The [AppError](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/AppError.js#10-19) hierarchy is clean and substitutable:
```
AppError (base)
├── ValidationError (400)
├── UnauthorizedError (401)
├── ForbiddenError (403)
├── NotFoundError (404)
├── ConflictError (409)
└── InternalError (500)
```
All can be thrown interchangeably and caught by [errorHandler.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/errorHandler.js). No behavioral surprises.

**Minor Issue:** [NotFoundError](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/AppError.js#50-55) constructor takes a `resource` string and generates `"${resource} not found"`, but some usages pass full messages like `'Event not found'` — resulting in `"Event not found not found"`. This subtle inconsistency violates LSP expectations.

---

### I — Interface Segregation Principle: **5/10** ⚠️

**Problem:** [event.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/event.service.js) exports a fat interface:
```js
module.exports = {
  createEventFromNoting, getEventDetails, validateEventRequiredFields,
  updateEvent, publishEvent, listEvents, registerForEvent,
  getMyRegistrations, getEventStatistics, assignVolunteer,
  scanQRCode, getEventRegistrations, getRegistrationDetails,
  getRegistrationFilterOptions, getEventVolunteers, getVolunteerActivity,
  getMyVolunteerAssignments, getMyVolunteerActivity, getEventFeedback,
};
```
A controller that only needs [listEvents](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/event.service.js#798-1006) must [require()](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js#251-314) a module that also pulls in statistics computation, raw SQL, volunteer management, and QR scanning. **Every consumer is forced to depend on the entire 1,279-line module.**

**Same issue with** [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js) — a module needing only [protect](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js#19-188) must import a file containing IPR, research, DSW, gate entry, and event-specific permission logic.

---

### D — Dependency Inversion Principle: **5/10** ⚠️

**Problem — Hard-coupled to Prisma:**
Every service file does:
```js
const prisma = require('../../../shared/config/database');
```
This is a **direct import of a concrete implementation** — making it impossible to:
- Swap the database for testing (no dependency injection)
- Mock Prisma in unit tests without `jest.mock` hacks
- Use a different ORM or database
- Test business logic in isolation

**Problem — Hard-coupled to Redis:**
```js
const cache = require('../../../shared/config/redis');
```
Same issue. Cache is a concrete singleton, not an injected dependency.

**Problem — Hard-coupled to `process.env`:**
[payment.service.js:27-31](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/payment.service.js#L27-L31) reads `process.env.RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` directly. Environment configuration should be injected, not read inline.

