## 🔒 Security Analysis

### ✅ Good Practices
- **Helmet.js** configured for security headers
- **HMAC-SHA256 signature verification** for Razorpay payments — properly prevents tampering
- **Webhook signature verification** separate from client-side verification
- **HTML sanitization** ([sanitizeHtml](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/validators.js#26-41)) strips script/iframe/object/embed tags and event handlers
- **Rate limiting** on login and public endpoints
- **JWT token verification** with proper error handling
- **CORS configuration** with whitelisted origins

### ⚠️ Concerns

| Issue | Severity | Location |
|-------|----------|----------|
| **Regex-based HTML sanitization** | 🔴 High | [validators.js:29-39](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/validators.js#L29-L39) — Regex cannot reliably sanitize HTML. Use [DOMPurify](https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify) or [sanitize-html](https://github.com/apostrophecms/sanitize-html) instead. Attackers can bypass regex with encoding tricks. |
| **`$queryRawUnsafe` usage** | 🟡 Medium | [eventHelpers.js:19-25](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/utils/eventHelpers.js#L19-L25) — Uses parameterized `$1` placeholders ✅, but `$queryRawUnsafe` is still riskier than `$queryRaw` with tagged templates |
| **Sensitive info in error responses** | 🟡 Medium | [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/middleware/auth.js) returns `checkedVariants` and `requiredPermissions` in 403 responses — leaks internal permission naming to attackers |
| **Dev secret fallback** | 🟡 Medium | [app.config.js:14](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/config/app.config.js#L14) — `'dev-only-insecure-secret'` fallback in JWT config. Fail-fast check exists for production, but development mode still uses a guessable static secret |
| **No request body size limits** | 🟡 Medium | [server.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/server.js) uses `express.json()` and `express.urlencoded()` without explicit body size limits |
| **Password policy too weak** | 🟢 Low | [validators.js:16-18](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/shared/utils/validators.js#L16-L18) — Only requires 8 chars with one letter and one number. No uppercase/special char requirement. |

