## ⚡ Performance Analysis

### ✅ Smart Optimizations Already Present
- **Raw SQL** for [getEventStatistics](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/event.service.js#1143-1259) — avoids N+1 and over-fetching
- **`Promise.all`** for parallelizing independent queries (used consistently in [team.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/team.service.js), [registration.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/registration.service.js), [payment.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/payment.service.js))
- **Redis caching** with event-specific TTLs and proper invalidation
- **Lean queries** with `select` to minimize data transfer
- **`buildVisibilityFilter`** pushes filtering to the database layer

### ⚠️ Anti-Patterns

| Issue | Location | Impact |
|-------|----------|--------|
| **Sequential N+1 in transaction** | [registration.service.js:433-457](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/registration.service.js#L433-L457) — Loops through `EventCustomField` array and does individual `upsert` per field inside a transaction | Medium — could use `createMany` or batch upsert |
| **Repeated event lookups** | Every function resolves `eventId` separately, even when called from the same request flow | Medium — a request touching payment → team → registration does 3 separate event lookups |
| **No pagination on team queries** | [team.service.js](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/team.service.js) — [getTeamsLookingForMembers](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/services/team.service.js#1044-1165) fetches all teams without cursor or pagination | Medium for popular events |
| **[generateRegistrationId](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/utils/eventHelpers.js#38-69) race condition** | [eventHelpers.js:46-68](file:///c:/Users/anwee/Desktop_1/Learning-Season/SGT_1v/Sgt-Ums/backend/src/modules/event-management/utils/eventHelpers.js#L46-L68) — Comment says "atomic" but uses `SELECT MAX + 1` pattern without database-level locking | High under concurrent registrations — two requests can get the same ID |

